WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:03.460
Welcome to the Firehouse fifty-one
training department in Resgrid.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:08.010
This walkthrough uses the real application
running from the project code, with

3
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.250
fictional personnel and exercise data.

4
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.569
We will follow a few connected tasks:
organizing the department,

5
00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:19.360
dispatching a call, staffing a deployment,
and documenting readiness.

6
00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:25.090
The personnel page brings Wallace Boden,
Kelly Severide, Stella Kidd, Sylvie Brett,

7
00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:27.320
and their colleagues into one roster.

8
00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:32.129
Stations, groups, and personnel roles
describe where each member belongs.

9
00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:36.899
Staffing and response status answer
different questions: who is available,

10
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.390
and what are they doing now?

11
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.960
Keep those assignments accurate before
depending on the roster.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:47.259
The apparatus list includes Engine
fifty-one, Truck eighty-one, Squad

13
00:00:47.259 --> 00:00:49.330
three, and Ambulance sixty-one.

14
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.260
The unit configuration connects an
apparatus to its station

15
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.069
and defines its crew positions.

16
00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.520
A reserve engine is marked out of service
so it remains

17
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.270
visible without appearing ready.

18
00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:04.379
These distinctions help departments avoid
confusing a listed resource

19
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.899
with an available resource.

20
00:01:06.029 --> 00:01:08.059
Now create a Medical training call.

21
00:01:08.519 --> 00:01:13.320
Enter a clear name, priority, incident
identifier, and a short description.

22
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.960
Use the recipient controls to select
Ambulance sixty-one.

23
00:01:17.529 --> 00:01:21.569
After saving the dispatch, the dashboard
shows the ambulance as Responding.

24
00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:25.040
That confirms the recorded dispatch and
status transition.

25
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:30.909
This isolated environment does not send
real pages, texts, or push notifications.

26
00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:34.039
Open the saved call to review the incident
details.

27
00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:38.590
At the end of the exercise, open Close
Call, choose the completion

28
00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.930
outcome, and enter the closeout notes.

29
00:01:41.269 --> 00:01:44.739
The saved record now shows Closed and
retains the narrative.

30
00:01:45.069 --> 00:01:48.560
Departments gain a consistent handoff from
intake to review,

31
00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:51.980
with a record of what was entered and when
the call was completed.

32
00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.580
For planned coverage, create a deployment
and link the community standby call.

33
00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:00.729
Enter the operational dates, then add
Ambulance sixty-one

34
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.439
and Sylvie Brett to the roster.

35
00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.559
The deployment summary brings the assigned
people and apparatus together.

36
00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:09.110
This example is operational only.

37
00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.110
Finance, reimbursement, and external
ordering require their own

38
00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.289
configuration and supporting evidence.

39
00:02:15.359 --> 00:02:17.879
Readiness starts with an approved
checklist.

40
00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.019
Open the Engine fifty-one daily check,
choose the apparatus,

41
00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.899
and answer each required item.

42
00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:27.870
Submit the completed check, then inspect
its detail page.

43
00:02:28.259 --> 00:02:31.630
This demonstration shows three passing
answers and a submitted

44
00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.390
score of one hundred percent.

45
00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:38.310
A recorded pass is evidence of the entered
check; a failed item would still

46
00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.370
need an assigned repair or follow-up.

47
00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.339
Finally, the Records workspace contains a
saved training draft

48
00:02:44.339 --> 00:02:48.549
with an instructor, participant,
apparatus, dates, and narrative.

49
00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.299
Inventory shows the imported demonstration
balances, and the

50
00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:54.570
calendar shows upcoming exercises.

51
00:02:54.969 --> 00:02:57.969
These views connect daily activity with
follow-up work.

52
00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:01.959
Use this department to practise, verify
the saved result, and

53
00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:03.920
decide who owns the next action.

